HitX is an iOS App ballistic calculator designed for a projectile trajectory forecast to adjust the windage and elevation using an optical scope device. The application helps the shooter save a lot of time and cartridges during long-range shooting sessions. 

The key features:
• Accurate projectile trajectory calculations based on verified algorithms and formulas;
• More than 3300 factory-made cartridges and bullets in the database (with G1 and G7 drag functions);
• More than 1300 optical scope devices in the database;
• Full data gathering automation (weather, geo, cartridges, bullets, scopes, etc.);
• The App supports Imperial and Metric units of measurements. The App provides calculation results in MRAD(MIL), MOA, cm, in, clicks;
• Coriolis and Derivation forces inclusion;
• Excellent user interface designed by shooters for shooters;
• Multi-Language App;
• Minimum battery consumption (AMOLED and OLED displays only);
• Help is available on each screen to get desired information and hints related to the interface;

Real shooters verified all algorithms and formulas we use in HitX. An excellent user interface is also is designed by shooters to provide fast and easy long-range shooting sessions. You always get ready to shoot accurately or to zero a rifle in a few seconds!

HitX ballistic calculator uses the capacity of modern mobile technologies such as device barometer, camera, GPS navigation for data gathering automation. The usage of predefined data from the optical scope device database and bullet database makes the user's life easier. It helps to avoid any data entry mistakes during shooting and/or rifle zeroing. 

HitX is a community-driven application focused on the best shooter experience possible, along with customer service.

Required permissions: 
GPS, device camera, internet connection, internal barometer.

An Apple Watch (standalone, no phone required), iPhone and iPad app for using Alexa.

Control your home devices, ask general questions, add and remove items to your shopping list and set timers etc.  It is an Alexa implementation.  On your wrist.

There are nine things you should know before getting this app:

1. The Series 4 watch and newer are supported;
2. Your phone controls installation of the app to the watch, not the app.  Put your watch on a charger to speed up install time;
3. Not all audio content can be supported.  Amazon don't allow third-party apps such as this app to play music, audio books or some daily-news content, make announcements or drop-in;
4. You can use a Siri Shortcut to launch the app and start speaking, just by raising your wrist on Apple Watch.  See the support page on how to configure;
5. All watch complication types are supported, including those really weird ones.  Also you can change the complication icon under Settings;
6. The watch app can listen automatically on launch. There is an option under settings to do the same thing on the iPhone;
7. If the weather or time are wrong, ensure you've enabled Location access in the Alexa app to the "Voice in a Can" device, and that you have granted Location permissions to the app on your phone;
8. You don't have to say "Alexa" ... just speak your command when the app is listening;
9. You can change the language that you speak and hear responses in, under "Settings" on the watch and phone.  Only languages supported by Alexa are supported. The language should be set automatically.

If you have questions or any support issues please don't hesitate to email damian@voiceinacan.com ... you should get a response within 24 hours, and often in minutes.

